# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp

# Node.
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# Local staging the installer writes; never part of the source tree.
.install/
*.log

# Verification residue (a suite that throws mid-run can leave these behind).
# /%SystemDrive%/ is an unexpanded cmd-style %VAR% one: something ran with this
# repo as its CWD and built the Windows chain under a literal folder name. The
# writer is unidentified. This rule HIDES the path; it protects nothing and
# schedules no cleanup — measured in a scratch repo: with no rule `git clean
# -fdn` reports the empty directory, with the rule it does not, and `git status
# --ignored -uall` does not list it either (git cannot see an empty directory).
# Only `git clean -Xdn` shows what is being kept out. That is the intent — the
# junk must never be committed — but finding it again is a manual job.
/tmp-probe/
/%SystemDrive%/
_debug-*.mjs

# A one-off client probe (it polls /plugins/events on a port that no longer
# serves). Untracked, harmless, and nothing ignored it — one `git add -A` would
# have committed it.
.icon-probe.mjs

# Bytecode cache from py_compile on the shipped bridge source. Hygiene only:
# "files" in package.json whitelists all of lib/, and npm cannot exclude a
# files-included path through .gitignore — scripts.prepack is what keeps the
# cache out of the tarball. This rule keeps it out of git, nothing more.
lib/wsl/__pycache__/

# Release artifacts. `npm pack` output is reproducible from this tree and is
# never part of it — and a stale one is worse than noise: an older tarball can be
# a build that cannot load at all, sitting there installable.
*.tgz

# Verification receipts (`verify-all.mjs --receipt`). A receipt describes ONE
# machine's run — which suites passed, which skipped and why — so committing it
# would make a claim about this operator's setup look like a claim about the
# project. It is produced to be pasted into an issue, not stored.
verify-receipt*.json
.receipt-check.json

# The diagram tooling's own working directory (archify inputs, receipts, the
# sdd evidence tree). It is a TOOL WORKSPACE, not source: `release-check.mjs`
# already refuses to ship anything under `.superpowers/`, and `docs/diagrams.md`
# records that its measurement artefacts are observation, not deliverables.
# Ignoring it here keeps `git status` readable — it is ~37 MB across 1000 files.
.superpowers/
